## Course Overview

This course provides a comprehensive introduction to safety-critical control architectures in railway engineering, train protection systems (ATP/ATO/ATS), and fail-safe interlocking logic design.

- Learn vital logic design and railway interlocking principles
- Understand automatic train control frameworks (ETCS / CBTC)
- Compare fixed block vs. moving block signaling architectures
- Apply Safety Integrity Level (SIL) standards to railway control design

## Prerequisites

- Control Systems Theory
- Logic Design Fundamentals

## Textbooks

- "Railway Signalling and Interlocking" by Gregor Theiss
- "Principles of Railway Location and Design" by Siripreet Singh

